2D CIRCUIT RACER — FULL RECREATION SPEC
=======================================
Single-file Python + pygame arcade racer. Goal: another implementer (human or LLM)
should be able to rebuild a playable equivalent from this document alone.

1. PURPOSE AND SCOPE
--------------------
A top-down 2D racing game.
- New closed track every race (not a fixed figure-8).
- Track fills most of a 1280x720 window and is relatively long.
- Mix of loops and straightaways; self-crossings become overpasses.
- Oil slicks.
- Cars collide with each other: they shove apart and lose speed; they do not explode.
- One human, or two humans plus AI.
- Each race is 5 laps.
- Four gears. Gears shift AUTOMATICALLY. Player does not shift manually.
- Holding accelerate builds speed; release = coast; down = brake.

2. DEPENDENCIES AND ENTRY
-------------------------
- Python 3.
- pygame.
- One file, e.g. racer.py.
- Window: 1280 x 720, 60 FPS, caption "2D Circuit Racer".
- Entry: if __name__ == "__main__": main()

3. CONSTANTS
------------
W, H          = 1280, 720
FPS           = 60
LAPS          = 5
N_AI          = 2
TRACK_W       = 52          # asphalt ribbon width in pixels
CAR_R         = 11          # collision radius

GEAR_MAX[0..4] = unused, 160, 250, 340, 430    # top speed px/s for gears 1-4
GEAR_ACC[0..4] = unused, 320, 260, 200, 150    # accel px/s^2 while throttle held
BRAKE          = 420        # px/s^2 when brake held
COAST_DRAG     = 28         # px/s^2 when neither throttle nor brake
TURN           = 3.1        # rad/s base steer rate

Car colors (RGBA not required):
  P1     (230, 70, 70)
  P2     (70, 140, 255)
  CPU-1  (255, 200, 50)
  CPU-2  (90, 220, 130)

Grass / background fill: (26, 108, 50)

4. GAME FLOW
------------
Modes: "menu" | "race" | "results"

MENU
- Title: "2D CIRCUIT RACER"
- Short rules text (new track each race, auto gears, oil, crashes dump speed).
- Keys:
    1     start race: P1 vs N_AI computers
    2     start race: P1 + P2 + N_AI computers
    ESC   quit application

RACE
- Generate a fresh track + oil list.
- Spawn cars near waypoint 0, slightly offset left/right of centerline, facing track tangent.
- Run simulation and draw until every human car has finished 5 laps
  (AI may still be running; ending when humans are done is enough).
- ESC returns to menu (abandon race).

RESULTS
- Dark translucent overlay.
- "FINISH"
- Cars sorted: finished first (by finish timestamp), then unfinished by laps/waypoint.
- Show time in seconds with 2 decimals for finishers.
- ENTER or ESC → menu.

5. CONTROLS (RACE)
------------------
Gears are never mapped to keys.

Player 1
  Up arrow      accelerate (throttle = 1 else 0)
  Down arrow    brake      (brake = 1 else 0)
  Left / Right  steer      (-1, 0, or +1; both = 0)
  no keys       coast

Player 2 (only if mode 2)
  W / S         accel / brake
  A / D         steer

If neither accel nor brake: apply COAST_DRAG only.

6. TRACK GENERATION (NEW EVERY RACE)
------------------------------------
Must NOT be a single canned figure-8. Must use most of the screen.

6.1 Control points
- Margin m = 70 px from every window edge.
- Build an irregular closed loop of 8..12 control points:
    angle_i = i/n * 2π + small jitter ±0.18
    radius_x = uniform(0.40W, 0.47W)
    radius_y = uniform(0.36H, 0.44H)
    Occasionally shrink one radius to stretch a side into a longer straight.
    x = clamp(W/2 + cos(angle)*rx, m, W-m)
    y = clamp(0.52H + sin(angle)*ry, m, H-m)

6.2 Extra loops
- Insert 1..3 extra detour loops.
- Pick a random existing control point (px, py).
- Build 5..7 points around it with radius 70..130, slightly elliptical,
  clamped to the margin, and splice them into the control list at that index.
- This creates extra circuits attached to the main loop.

6.3 Smoothing
- Catmull-Rom spline through the closed control list.
- Adaptive samples: more samples on long segments (about 8–14+ per span,
  scaled by segment length / 140).
- Drop samples closer than ~10 px so the polyline is not over-dense.
- Result: list of (x, y) along a long closed ribbon.

6.4 Overpasses / layers
- Each sample gets layer 0 by default.
- Detect self-intersections between non-adjacent polyline segments
  (skip segments whose index distance along the loop is small, e.g. < 12).
- When two segments cross, mark a short window of samples on ONE of the
  two strands as layer 1 (e.g. indices j-4 .. j+4).
- Layer 1 is the overpass. Cars on different layers do not collide.
- Stored points: (x, y, layer)

6.5 Oil
- 5..9 patches.
- Each: (x, y, layer, radius) with radius 16..26, lightly jittered off a
  random track sample, same layer as that sample.

6.6 Start / finish
- Waypoint index 0 is the line.
- Draw a white stripe across the track width using the local tangent’s
  perpendicular.

7. DRAWING THE TRACK
--------------------
Background grass first.
Then stroke the polyline twice:
  Layer 0: asphalt (46,50,56), thin light edge (210,210,220), width TRACK_W
  Layer 1: slightly lighter asphalt (64,68,76), yellow edge (240,210,70),
           width TRACK_W+2
Draw consecutive samples with pygame.draw.line (round caps look better if available).
Oil: dark green disc + lighter inner disc.
Start line last among track elements.
Cars drawn after track: all layer-0 cars, then all layer-1 cars
(so overpass cars render on top).

8. CAR STATE
------------
x, y, angle (radians, 0 = east, increases clockwise-or-CCW consistent with atan2)
layer
speed (px/s, >= 0)
gear in {1,2,3,4}
wp          nearest track-sample index (hinted search around last index)
last_wp     previous wp, for lap wrap detection
laps        completed full passes of the start line (0 at start)
finished    bool
finish_time pygame.time.get_ticks() when laps reaches LAPS
oil_t       seconds of remaining oil effect
crash_t     seconds of remaining crash stun
ai          bool
name, color

Spawn:
  angle = tangent at start index
  position = waypoint + perpendicular * offset
  offsets like -14 / +14 for humans, ±18 for AI
  AI start indices a few samples behind 0 so they line up in a pack
  (e.g. len(pts) - 8*(k+1))

9. PHYSICS (FIXED DT ~ 1/60)
----------------------------
Skip movement logic if finished except speed *= 0.95 (rollout).

Timers:
  oil_t  = max(0, oil_t - dt)
  crash_t = max(0, crash_t - dt)

Oil trigger: if same layer and distance to oil center < radius + CAR_R,
set oil_t = 0.4

Speed:
  if throttle and crash_t <= 0:  speed += GEAR_ACC[gear] * dt
  elif brake:                    speed -= BRAKE * dt
  else:                          speed -= COAST_DRAG * dt
  if oil_t > 0:                  speed *= max(0, 1 - 1.6*dt)
  if crash_t > 0:                speed *= 0.90
  speed = clamp(speed, 0, GEAR_MAX[gear])

Auto-shift AFTER integrating speed:
  if gear < 4 and speed > GEAR_MAX[gear] * 0.88:          gear += 1
  elif gear > 1 and speed < GEAR_MAX[gear-1] * 0.62:      gear -= 1
  then clamp speed again to new GEAR_MAX[gear]

Steering:
  grip = 1 / (1 + speed/300)
  if on oil: add a time-based wobble to steer (e.g. sin(ticks*0.025)*1.1)
             and multiply grip by 0.3
  angle += steer * TURN * (0.35 + 0.65*grip) * dt
  (keeps a little steer authority at low speed)

Integrate:
  x += cos(angle) * speed * dt
  y += sin(angle) * speed * dt

Nearest waypoint:
  search indices hint-10 .. hint+21 around last wp (wrapped).
  layer = pts[wp].layer

Soft track walls:
  If distance from car to nearest sample > TRACK_W * 0.58,
  pull toward the sample and multiply speed by ~0.99.
  Do not hard-stop the car; the original bug report was “cars never moved”,
  so walls must not cancel throttle.

Lap detection:
  n = number of samples
  if last_wp > 0.82n AND wp < 0.18n: laps += 1
  if laps >= LAPS: finished = True, record finish_time
  last_wp = wp

10. CAR–CAR COLLISION
---------------------
Only if other is not self AND other.layer == self.layer.
If distance < 2.2 * CAR_R:
  push both apart equally along the contact normal
  both speed *= 0.55
  both crash_t = 0.3
No elimination, no spinning out as a hard state machine; just slow / brief stun.
Different-layer cars pass through each other (overpass).

11. AI
------
Look-ahead sample: wp + 10 + int(speed/70)  (wrapped).
desired_heading = atan2(target - position)
heading error wrapped to [-π, π]
steer = clamp(error * 1.8, -1, 1)
accel = 1.0 if abs(error) < 0.75 else 0.45
brake = 1.0 if abs(error) > 1.15 and speed > 170 else 0
AI uses the same update() as humans, including auto-shift.

12. CAR DRAWING
---------------
Small 4-vertex trapezoid / capsule oriented by angle:
  nose +16 along heading, tail -12, half-width 8.
  Fill with car color, 2 px dark outline.

13. HUD (RACE)
--------------
Top-left:
  "{LAPS} LAP RACE   {elapsed.1f}s"
  Standings sorted by (-laps, -wp, -speed):
    "{place}. {name}  L{current}/{LAPS}  G{gear}  {int speed}"
    or "FIN" if finished.
Name column short (P1, P2, CPU-1, CPU-2).

14. RESULTS SORT
----------------
Key: (0 if finished else 1, finish_time or +inf, -laps, -wp)
Time shown as (finish_time - race_start_ticks) / 1000, two decimals.

15. IMPLEMENTATION NOTES / PITFALLS
-----------------------------------
- Throttle must produce visible motion within a fraction of a second from
  standstill in gear 1. Do not apply heavy friction while throttle is held.
- Do not require a clutch or manual shift; that was why cars “never moved”.
- Window focus: arrow keys only work if the pygame window is focused.
- Track search must be local/wrapped; a full scan every frame is OK but slower.
- Crossing test must ignore adjacent segments or the ribbon will flag itself.
- Keep simulation deterministic-enough per seed if you add seeding; default
  can use unseeded random.
- No need for camera follow; world == screen, track already fills the window.
- No sprites required; primitives only.
- Do not print copyrighted assets; generate geometry only.

16. ACCEPTANCE CHECKLIST
------------------------
[ ] Menu 1 and 2 start different participant sets.
[ ] Holding Up moves P1 immediately; release coasts; Down brakes hard.
[ ] Left/Right rotate the car; motion follows heading.
[ ] Gear number on HUD climbs 1→4 as speed rises and drops when slow.
[ ] Each race’s track is a different long loop with extra loops + straights.
[ ] Track uses most of 1280x720 with ~70 px grass margin.
[ ] Yellow-edged strand appears where the path crosses; cars on that strand
    draw above and do not collide with underpass cars.
[ ] Green oil patches make the car slide / wobble and bleed speed.
[ ] Two cars overlapping on the same layer bounce and both slow.
[ ] Race ends after 5 completed laps for human(s); results list times.
[ ] ESC from race/results returns to menu; ESC on menu quits.